---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfessionalService',
  name: 'Jacob Chesslo — LGBTQ+ & Lifestyle Tech Consulting',
  description:
    'Tech consulting for LGBTQ+, kink, and lifestyle communities. Web development, apps, community platforms — built by someone in these spaces.',
  url: 'https://jacobchesslo.com/consulting/lifestyle',
  email: 'jacobchesslo@gmail.com',
  founder: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Jacob Chesslo',
    url: 'https://jacobchesslo.com',
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="LGBTQ+ & Lifestyle Tech Consulting — Jacob Chesslo"
  description="Jacob Chesslo builds web, apps, and community platforms for LGBTQ+, kink, and lifestyle communities — software from someone actually in these spaces."
  fullWidth={true}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- ── SCROLL SCENE ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div class="scroll-scene" id="lifestyle-scene">
    <div class="sticky-stage">
      <canvas id="lifestyle-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

      <div class="text-pill">
        <div class="pill-header">
          <a href="/consulting" class="back-link">&larr; Consulting</a>
          <span class="page-tag">LGBTQ+ &amp; Lifestyle</span>
          <h1 class="page-title">Tech built<br /><span class="accent">for your world.</span></h1>
        </div>
        <div class="pill-body">
          <p class="page-sub">
            Web, apps, and community platforms for LGBTQ+, kink, and lifestyle communities. Built by
            someone who lives in these spaces.
          </p>
          <a href="mailto:jacobchesslo@gmail.com" class="cta-btn">Let's talk &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="phase-label" id="lifestyle-phase">isolated individuals</div>
      <div class="scroll-hint" id="lifestyle-hint">scroll to explore &darr;</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── CONTENT ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <article class="consult-body">
    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Why this matters</h2>
      <p>
        Most tech vendors treat LGBTQ+ and kink communities as edge cases to accommodate, not people
        to build for. The result is software that technically works but misses everything that
        actually matters — the culture, the trust requirements, the privacy needs, the specific ways
        people in these spaces connect and organize.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm not coming in as an outsider. I'm queer, I'm in kink and lifestyle communities, and I've
        spent years running LGBTQ+ organizations. I know what you actually need because I use and
        depend on this kind of software too.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="divider-line"></div>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-heading">What I can help with</h2>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <div class="cap-card">
          <div class="cap-title">Web &amp; App Development</div>
          <div class="cap-body">
            Full-stack web applications, landing pages, member portals. Modern stack (TypeScript,
            Astro, React/SolidJS) — fast, accessible, and actually maintained.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cap-card">
          <div class="cap-title">Community Platforms</div>
          <div class="cap-body">
            Member management, events, forums, onboarding flows. Spaces that feel right to the
            people in them — not a generic SaaS product with your logo on it.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cap-card">
          <div class="cap-title">Privacy &amp; Trust</div>
          <div class="cap-body">
            Members in these communities have real reasons to care about data privacy. I build with
            that as a first-class concern, not an afterthought.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cap-card">
          <div class="cap-title">Event Tech</div>
          <div class="cap-body">
            Registration, waivers, scheduling, check-in flows. The operational side of running
            events — built for the reality of how these events actually run.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="divider-line"></div>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2 class="section-heading">Good fit for</h2>
      <ul class="fit-list">
        <li>LGBTQ+ organizations or community groups that have outgrown their current tools</li>
        <li>Kink or lifestyle event organizers who need better event infrastructure</li>
        <li>Small businesses serving these communities that need a real web presence</li>
        <li>
          Anyone who's tired of explaining their community's needs from scratch to every vendor
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="divider-line"></div>

    <section class="cta-section">
      <p class="cta-note">
        This is a newer direction for me, so I'm starting by having real conversations — no
        packages, no rate cards. If you have something you want to build or fix, reach out and let's
        see if it's a fit.
      </p>
      <a href="mailto:jacobchesslo@gmail.com" class="cta-btn-body">jacobchesslo@gmail.com</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script>
  const scene = document.getElementById('lifestyle-scene')! as HTMLElement;
  const canvas = document.getElementById('lifestyle-canvas')! as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const phaseEl = document.getElementById('lifestyle-phase')! as HTMLElement;
  const hintEl = document.getElementById('lifestyle-hint')! as HTMLElement;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!;

  const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  const PHASES = [
    'isolated individuals',
    'finding community',
    'connections forming',
    'thriving together',
  ];

  // Pride rainbow — one hue per cluster
  const CLUSTER_COLORS = [
    'oklch(62% 0.25 18', // red
    'oklch(66% 0.22 55', // orange
    'oklch(82% 0.19 98', // yellow
    'oklch(64% 0.21 148', // green
    'oklch(62% 0.21 245', // blue
    'oklch(62% 0.22 295', // violet
  ];

  let W = 0,
    H = 0;
  let rawProgress = 0,
    displayProgress = 0;

  // ── Cluster setup ─────────────────────────────────────────
  const CLUSTER_N = 6;
  const NODES_EACH = 15;

  interface Node {
    rx: number;
    ry: number; // random start
    cx: number;
    cy: number; // cluster center
    tx: number;
    ty: number; // target within cluster
    x: number;
    y: number; // current
    vx: number;
    vy: number;
    cluster: number;
    ph: number;
    sp: number;
  }

  let nodes: Node[] = [];

  function clusterCenter(i: number): { x: number; y: number } {
    const angle = (i / CLUSTER_N) * Math.PI * 2 - Math.PI / 2;
    const rx = Math.min(W, H) * 0.28;
    const ry = Math.min(W, H) * 0.25;
    return {
      x: W / 2 + Math.cos(angle) * rx,
      y: H / 2 + Math.sin(angle) * ry,
    };
  }

  function initNodes() {
    nodes = [];
    for (let ci = 0; ci < CLUSTER_N; ci++) {
      const { x: cx, y: cy } = clusterCenter(ci);
      for (let j = 0; j < NODES_EACH; j++) {
        const angle = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
        const dist = 20 + Math.random() * 50;
        nodes.push({
          rx: Math.random() * W,
          ry: Math.random() * H,
          cx,
          cy,
          tx: cx + Math.cos(angle) * dist,
          ty: cy + Math.sin(angle) * dist,
          x: 0,
          y: 0,
          vx: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.4,
          vy: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.4,
          cluster: ci,
          ph: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,
          sp: 0.35 + Math.random() * 0.8,
        });
      }
    }
    nodes.forEach((n) => {
      n.x = n.rx;
      n.y = n.ry;
    });
  }

  let resizeTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;
  function resize() {
    const newW = canvas.offsetWidth,
      newH = canvas.offsetHeight;
    const widthChanged = Math.abs(newW - W) > 20;
    W = newW;
    H = newH;
    if (widthChanged || nodes.length === 0) {
      canvas.width = Math.round(W * devicePixelRatio);
      canvas.height = Math.round(H * devicePixelRatio);
      ctx.scale(devicePixelRatio, devicePixelRatio);
      initNodes();
    }
  }

  function eio(t: number) {
    return t < 0.5 ? 2 * t * t : -1 + (4 - 2 * t) * t;
  }

  function draw(ts: number) {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);

    displayProgress += (rawProgress - displayProgress) * (reduced ? 1 : 0.045);
    const prog = reduced ? 1 : displayProgress;
    const gather = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (prog - 0.1) / 0.3)); // nodes converge to clusters
    const intra = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (prog - 0.48) / 0.24)); // within-cluster connections
    const inter = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (prog - 0.78) / 0.2)); // between-cluster bridges

    // Update node positions
    for (const n of nodes) {
      if (gather < 1) {
        const drift = (1 - gather) * 0.5;
        n.rx += n.vx * drift;
        n.ry += n.vy * drift;
        if (n.rx < 0 || n.rx > W) n.vx *= -1;
        if (n.ry < 0 || n.ry > H) n.vy *= -1;
      }
      const e = eio(gather);
      n.x = n.rx + (n.tx - n.rx) * e;
      n.y = n.ry + (n.ty - n.ry) * e;
    }

    // Within-cluster connections (cluster color)
    if (intra > 0) {
      const maxD = 90;
      for (let i = 0; i < nodes.length; i++) {
        for (let j = i + 1; j < nodes.length; j++) {
          if (nodes[i].cluster !== nodes[j].cluster) continue;
          const dx = nodes[j].x - nodes[i].x,
            dy = nodes[j].y - nodes[i].y;
          const d = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
          if (d < maxD) {
            const a = (1 - d / maxD) * intra * 0.55;
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.strokeStyle = `${CLUSTER_COLORS[nodes[i].cluster]} / ${a})`;
            ctx.lineWidth = 0.6 + inter * 0.3;
            ctx.moveTo(nodes[i].x, nodes[i].y);
            ctx.lineTo(nodes[j].x, nodes[j].y);
            ctx.stroke();
          }
        }
      }
    }

    // Between-cluster bridges (gradient between adjacent cluster colors)
    if (inter > 0) {
      for (let ci = 0; ci < CLUSTER_N; ci++) {
        const cj = (ci + 1) % CLUSTER_N;
        const aN = nodes.filter((n) => n.cluster === ci);
        const bN = nodes.filter((n) => n.cluster === cj);
        let best = Infinity,
          bai = 0,
          bbj = 0;
        for (let ai = 0; ai < aN.length; ai++) {
          for (let bj = 0; bj < bN.length; bj++) {
            const dx = bN[bj].x - aN[ai].x,
              dy = bN[bj].y - aN[ai].y;
            const d = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
            if (d < best) {
              best = d;
              bai = ai;
              bbj = bj;
            }
          }
        }
        const grad = ctx.createLinearGradient(aN[bai].x, aN[bai].y, bN[bbj].x, bN[bbj].y);
        grad.addColorStop(0, `${CLUSTER_COLORS[ci]} / ${inter * 0.4})`);
        grad.addColorStop(1, `${CLUSTER_COLORS[cj]} / ${inter * 0.4})`);
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.strokeStyle = grad;
        ctx.lineWidth = 0.8;
        ctx.setLineDash([3, 5]);
        ctx.moveTo(aN[bai].x, aN[bai].y);
        ctx.lineTo(bN[bbj].x, bN[bbj].y);
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.setLineDash([]);
      }
    }

    // Nodes (cluster color)
    for (const n of nodes) {
      const col = CLUSTER_COLORS[n.cluster];
      const pulse = Math.sin(ts * 0.001 * n.sp + n.ph) * 0.5 + 0.5;
      const baseA = 0.2 + gather * 0.45 + inter * 0.15;
      const r = 1.5 + pulse * 0.7 + inter * 0.8;

      if (intra > 0) {
        const gr = ctx.createRadialGradient(n.x, n.y, 0, n.x, n.y, r * 5);
        gr.addColorStop(0, `${col} / ${intra * 0.2})`);
        gr.addColorStop(1, 'transparent');
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(n.x, n.y, r * 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fillStyle = gr;
        ctx.fill();
      }

      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(n.x, n.y, r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fillStyle = `${col} / ${baseA + pulse * 0.12})`;
      ctx.fill();
    }

    // Phase label
    const idx = prog < 0.18 ? 0 : prog < 0.52 ? 1 : prog < 0.8 ? 2 : 3;
    if (phaseEl.dataset.idx !== String(idx)) {
      phaseEl.dataset.idx = String(idx);
      phaseEl.style.opacity = '0';
      setTimeout(() => {
        phaseEl.textContent = PHASES[idx];
        phaseEl.style.opacity = '1';
      }, 120);
    }

    hintEl.style.opacity = String(Math.max(0, 1 - prog * 18));
  }

  function updateProgress() {
    const rect = scene.getBoundingClientRect();
    const scrollable = scene.offsetHeight - window.innerHeight;
    if (scrollable > 0) rawProgress = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, -rect.top / scrollable));
  }

  resize();
  window.addEventListener(
    'resize',
    () => {
      clearTimeout(resizeTimer);
      resizeTimer = setTimeout(resize, 120);
    },
    { passive: true }
  );
  window.addEventListener('scroll', updateProgress, { passive: true });

  if (reduced) {
    rawProgress = 1;
    draw(0);
  } else {
    function tick(ts: number) {
      draw(ts);
      requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    }
    requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
</script>

<style>
  .scroll-scene {
    height: 420vh;
    position: relative;
  }

  .sticky-stage {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    height: 100vh;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  #lifestyle-canvas {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .sticky-stage::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 180px;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, var(--bg));
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .text-pill {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 3rem;
    left: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    max-width: 380px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    background: oklch(3% 0.006 264 / 0.78);
    backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .back-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color var(--dur-fast);
  }
  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--secondary);
  }

  .page-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.08;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .page-title .accent {
    color: var(--secondary);
  }

  .page-sub {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    color: oklch(78% 0.018 295);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .cta-btn {
    display: inline-block;
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--bg);
    background: var(--secondary);
    padding: 0.55rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      background var(--dur-fast),
      transform var(--dur-fast);
  }
  .cta-btn:hover {
    background: oklch(55% 0.24 340);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .phase-label {
    position: absolute;
    top: 5rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--secondary);
    white-space: nowrap;
    background: oklch(3% 0.006 264 / 0.72);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border: 1px solid oklch(63% 0.24 340 / 0.25);
    border-radius: 100px;
    padding: 0.45rem 1.1rem;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .scroll-hint {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 1.5rem;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
    z-index: 2;
    animation: hint-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes hint-pulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 0.35;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  /* ── Article body ─────────────────────────────────────── */
  .consult-body {
    max-width: 64ch;
    padding-left: max(1.5rem, calc((100% - 64ch) / 2));
    padding-right: max(1.5rem, calc((100% - 64ch) / 2));
    padding-top: 4rem;
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .divider-line {
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  .section-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .content-section p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .content-section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .capability-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .cap-card {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .cap-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--secondary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cap-body {
    font-size: 0.87rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .fit-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .fit-list li {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    position: relative;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .fit-list li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }

  .cta-section {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .cta-note {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .cta-btn-body {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--bg);
    background: var(--secondary);
    padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      background var(--dur-fast),
      transform var(--dur-fast);
  }
  .cta-btn-body:hover {
    background: oklch(55% 0.24 340);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .sticky-stage {
      height: 100svh;
    }

    .text-pill {
      display: contents;
    }

    .pill-header {
      position: absolute;
      top: 1.25rem;
      left: 1.25rem;
      max-width: calc(100vw - 2.5rem);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.4rem;
      background: oklch(3% 0.006 264 / 0.82);
      backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      z-index: 2;
    }

    .pill-body {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 1.5rem;
      left: 1.25rem;
      max-width: calc(100vw - 2.5rem);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      background: oklch(3% 0.006 264 / 0.82);
      backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      z-index: 2;
    }

    .page-title {
      font-size: 1.6rem;
    }

    .phase-label {
      display: none;
    }

    .scroll-hint {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
